# Cloudflare Pages response headers (paths are matched per rule; every matching
# rule's headers apply, and a header set twice is joined with a comma — for
# Content-Security-Policy that means both policies are enforced, so keep the
# demo's own meta policy and this one compatible).
#
# Baseline CSP for the whole site. The allowlists are the origins the built
# site actually loads (audited 2026-10-13 against `hugo --minify` output and
# the live edge, which also injects Cloudflare Web Analytics):
#   - script: gtag (googletagmanager.com) and the edge-injected
#     static.cloudflareinsights.com beacon. 'unsafe-inline' stays, as a
#     deliberate phase: gtag's bootstrap snippet, the 404 game and the
#     newsletter form's onsubmit are all inline. The demo pages narrow this on
#     their own meta policy, whose script-src is 'self' only, and the
#     intersection is what applies there.
#     The X embed (/setting-goals/, and the home/list pages that render its
#     full content) loads platform.x.com/widgets.js, which pulls its chunks
#     from platform.twitter.com and JSONP data from cdn.syndication.twimg.com.
#   - style/font: the Joan webfont pair, plus 'unsafe-inline' for the theme's
#     inline styles.
#   - img: 'self' plus data: URIs; https: is left open so a post can still
#     reference an external image without a header change.
#   - media: local files plus data: URIs — /web-uplift-report/ inlines a small
#     data:video/mp4 clip.
#   - frame: the embeds posts actually use (YouTube, paulkinlan.github.io,
#     esper.val.run, wasm-vs-js.paulkinlan-ea.deno.net, and X's
#     platform.twitter.com / platform.x.com / syndication.twitter.com post
#     iframes) and same-origin, for the in-page demos.
#   - connect: analytics endpoints, Cloudflare's beacon, and the three provider
#     APIs. The provider hosts are here because the demo's own meta policy
#     allows exactly one of them and policies intersect: without them in this
#     policy the demo's sends would be blocked outright.
#   - frame-ancestors is 'self', not 'none': /agent-do-my-agent-loop/ embeds
#     /where-prompts-run-demo/ in a same-origin iframe. Cross-origin framing is
#     still denied, which is what the clickjacking exposure was about.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://platform.x.com https://platform.twitter.com https://cdn.syndication.twimg.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; media-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://region1.google-analytics.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://api.anthropic.com https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com https://api.openai.com; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://www.youtube.com https://paulkinlan.github.io https://esper.val.run https://wasm-vs-js.paulkinlan-ea.deno.net https://platform.x.com https://platform.twitter.com https://syndication.twitter.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://buttondown.com; frame-ancestors 'self'

# Moderation page: keep it out of search indexes and caches. Access control is
# a Cloudflare Access application on /admin/* and /api/admin/*.
#
# The page is also the one place a narrower policy is worth the duplicate: the
# browser attaches the Access JWT to any same-origin request, so any script
# running in the admin page's context (a third-party analytics/widget dependency,
# or one inline-script injection anywhere on the origin) can call
# /api/admin/queue, /api/admin/moderate, /api/admin/trust, /api/admin/accounts or
# /api/admin/og with full moderator authority. Under the /* policy that script is
# allowed: script-src carries 'unsafe-inline' and five third-party hosts. This
# block repeats the baseline policy with script-src 'self' only, so a browser
# enforcing both policies allows neither inline script nor a third-party origin
# on the admin page, while every other directive keeps the baseline value. The
# admin page therefore loads no gtag, no inline speculation rules and no
# onload font promotion (head.html skips them for type: admin), and
# tests/security-headers.test.mjs fails the gate if this drifts from the /*
# policy in any directive other than script-src (aifocus-wwfp).
/admin/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Cache-Control: no-store
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; media-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://region1.google-analytics.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://api.anthropic.com https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com https://api.openai.com; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://www.youtube.com https://paulkinlan.github.io https://esper.val.run https://wasm-vs-js.paulkinlan-ea.deno.net https://platform.x.com https://platform.twitter.com https://syndication.twitter.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://buttondown.com; frame-ancestors 'self'

# Share-card pages exist only to be screenshotted into og:image
# (functions/og/[[path]].js); keep them out of search results.
/*/og-card.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
